  | available. -/
header:
  > def SeedOrbitAvailable (G : Set (V ≃ᵃ[ℝ] V)) (r : V →ᵃ[ℝ] ℝ) (avail : Set (V →ᵃ[ℝ] ℝ)) :
  >     Prop :=

### C015 [K] OrbitGeneration.lean:79 def BoundaryTransitive (round OG-1)
docstring OrbitGeneration.lean:78-78:
  | /-- **K∞-R, boundary transitivity**: a member of `G` carries any boundary state to any other. -/
header:
  > def BoundaryTransitive (Ω : Set V) (G : Set (V ≃ᵃ[ℝ] V)) : Prop :=

### C016 [K] OrbitGeneration.lean:83 def CoversBoundaryFrom (round OG-1)
docstring OrbitGeneration.lean:82-82:
  | /-- COVER: every boundary state is the image of `x₀` under a member of `G`. -/
header:
  > def CoversBoundaryFrom (Ω : Set V) (G : Set (V ≃ᵃ[ℝ] V)) (x₀ : V) : Prop :=

### C017 [K] TransitiveBody.lean:223 structure IsBodyGroup (round TRB-1)
docstring TransitiveBody.lean:221-222:
  | /-- **TRANS, the group clause.** `G` contains the identity, is closed under composition and
  | inversion, and every member maps `Ω` into `Ω`. -/
header:
  > structure IsBodyGroup (Ω : Set V) (G : Set (V ≃ᵃ[ℝ] V)) : Prop where
fields: one_mem@224, mul_mem@225, inv_mem@226, preserves@227

### C018 [K] TransitiveBody.lean:235 def TransBody (round TRB-1)
docstring TransitiveBody.lean:234-234:
  | /-- **TRANS.** A body group acting transitively on every boundary state of `Ω`. -/
header:
  > def TransBody (Ω : Set V) (G : Set (V ≃ᵃ[ℝ] V)) : Prop := IsBodyGroup Ω G ∧ BoundaryTransitive Ω G

